module colonyDensityDetection
module sixteenSrRNASequencing
module dropletViabilityDetection

manifest FetalCellSuspension
manifest BHIS_Medium
manifest GMM_Medium
manifest YCFA_Medium
manifest FC40_Oil
manifest HFE7500_Surfactant
manifest PFO_BreakingAgent
manifest FDA_PI_Stain
manifest ASF_FecalPellet
manifest BHIS_ASF_Medium
manifest DNAExtractionKit

instructions:

// ============================================================
// High-throughput Isolation and Sorting of Gut Microbes
// Reduce Biases of Traditional Cultivation Strategies
// Watterson et al., bioRxiv 2019 (doi: 10.1101/759969)
// Tay Lab / Eren Lab, University of Chicago
//
// Platform: Droplet microfluidic devices operated inside a
// vinyl anaerobic chamber (Coy Lab Products) supplied with
// 86% N2 / 10% O2 / 4% H2. O2 < 1 ppm maintained throughout.
// Droplets: ~65-115 pL picoliter droplets generated at a
// flow-focusing junction from liquid culture medium into oil
// (Bio-Rad Droplet Generation Oil for EvaGreen).
// Encapsulation: Fecal cell suspensions diluted such that
// ~20-30% of droplets contain exactly 1 live bacterial cell
// (Poisson statistics). Sorting: image-based wavelet OD
// measurement at ~30 Hz; no fluorescent reporters required.
//
// PROTOCOL STRUCTURE:
//   Phase 1 -- ASF model community validation (mouse gut,
//              8-species Altered Schaedler's Flora).
//   Phase 2 -- Human stool cultivation across 3 rich media
//              (BHIS, GMM, YCFA) vs. conventional agar plates.
//   Phase 3 -- Slow-growing colony sorting by colony density
//              (wavelet OD between 0.3 and 0.7) to further
//              amplify rare/low-abundance taxa (<1% in raw
//              stool amplified to >1% in sorted fraction).
//   Phase 4 -- Viability confirmation: streaking sorted
//              droplets onto agar plates for colony growth.
//
// NOTE ON ANAEROBIC ABSTRACTION: All `heat` statements at
// 37c model incubation inside the anaerobic chamber incubator.
// `mix` steps abstract microfluidic droplet generation and
// encapsulation events, not DMF electrode mixing.
//
// NOTE ON SORTING ABSTRACTION: The wavelet OD-based sorting
// (LabView, Basler camera at 925 Hz, 672x360 px, 59 us
// exposure; biorthogonal 3.1 wavelets, LLH subband) is
// abstracted as a `detect colonyDensityDetection` call
// followed by an if/else QC gate. Slow-growing colonies
// satisfy: 0.3 < waveletOD < 0.7.
//
// NOTE ON 16S AMPLICON ABSTRACTION: Post-cultivation DNA
// extraction (PFO emulsion break, DNeasy kit) and 16S V4
// amplicon sequencing (Illumina MiSeq 2x300 paired-end,
// primers from Caporaso et al. 2012) followed by MED/
// oligotyping analysis are abstracted as `detect
// sixteenSrRNASequencing` calls.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- anaerobic chamber init; ASF
//                             pure-strain droplet culture;
//                             ASF mixed-community culture;
//                             human stool BHIS droplets;
//                             human stool GMM droplets;
//                             human stool YCFA droplets;
//                             community richness QC gate
//   BB2  richnessPass      -- richnessSignal > 0: richness
//                             increase confirmed (droplets
//                             > plates); proceed to sorting
//   BB3  richnessFail      -- richnessSignal <= 0: no richness
//                             gain; drain cultivation output
//   BB4  richnessJoin      -- join: slow-grower sorting branch
//   BB5  sortingPass       -- sortingSignal > 0: low-density
//                             colonies successfully sorted;
//                             proceed to viability check
//   BB6  sortingFail       -- sortingSignal <= 0: no slow-
//                             growing colonies in fraction;
//                             drain sorted emulsion
//   BB7  sortingJoin       -- join: viability confirmation
//   BB8  viabilityPass     -- viabilitySignal > 0: bacteria
//                             viable after droplet cultivation;
//                             streak onto agar; dispose
//   BB9  viabilityFail     -- viabilitySignal <= 0: viability
//                             lost; drain
//   BB10 finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 1: Prime anaerobic chamber and microfluidic
//   device with FC-40 oil to establish anaerobic environment.
//   O2 < 1 ppm, H2 between 1.5-2.5% maintained throughout.
//   Devices fabricated by soft lithography (SU-8 3050 molds,
//   50 um channel height, PDMS bonded to glass). Channels
//   hydrophobized with Aquapel then Fluorinert FC-40.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

oilPrime      = dispense 1 units of FC40_Oil
surfactantPrime = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
devicePrime   = mix oilPrime with surfactantPrime for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 2: Prepare ASF model community from fecal
//   pellet (Taconic Biosciences). Dissociate 3 fecal pellets
//   in 5 mL BHIS-ASF medium, sediment fecal solids, collect
//   supernatant, store at -80 C in 25% glycerol/25% BHIS/
//   50% cell suspension. Dilute 50x for droplet generation.
//   Note: ASF 360 (L. intestinalis) not detected in pellets;
//   7 of 8 strains confirmed by species-specific PCR.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

asfFecalStock  = dispense 1 units of ASF_FecalPellet
asfMedium      = dispense 1 units of BHIS_ASF_Medium
asfDiluted     = mix asfFecalStock with asfMedium for 2s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 3: Generate ASF community droplets in anaerobic
//   chamber. Flow-focusing junction encapsulates ~20-30%
//   droplets with a single ASF cell (Poisson statistics).
//   Droplet volume: ~65-115 pL. Oil phase: HFE7500 with
//   2% surfactant. Droplet generation rate: ~0.5-1 mL
//   emulsion in 20 min to 1 hr.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

asfOilPhase    = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
asfDroplets    = mix asfDiluted with asfOilPhase for 3s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 4: Incubate ASF droplets at 37 C for 24 h
//   inside anaerobic chamber incubator. Single cells grow
//   clonally within confined droplet volumes, preventing
//   competitive overgrowth of fast-growing ASF 361
//   (L. murinus) over ASF 519 (P. goldsteinii) as occurs
//   in bulk broth. Extremely oxygen-sensitive species (ASF
//   356, 492, 500, 502) maintained below 1 ppm O2.
//   24 h = 1440 min.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

heat asfDroplets at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 1, STEP 5: Quantify ASF community composition by
//   droplet digital PCR (BioRad QX200). Species-specific
//   primers from Sarma-Rupavtarm et al. (2004). ddPCR mix:
//   10 uL QX200 ddPCR EvaGreen Supermix, 200 nM each primer,
//   thermocycle: 94 C 10 min; 35 cycles (94 C 1 min,
//   60 C 1 min, 72 C 2 min). Break emulsion with PFO before
//   DNA extraction (DNeasy Blood & Tissue Kit, 100 uL elution).
//   Expected: ASF 361 dominates bulk broth; droplets confine
//   ASF 361 and allow ASF 457 (34%) and ASF 519 (0.96%) to
//   reach higher relative abundance.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

asfBreakingAgent = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
asfKit           = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
asfBroken        = mix asfDroplets with asfBreakingAgent for 2s
asfDNA           = mix asfBroken with asfKit for 30m
asfComposition   = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on asfDNA for 30s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 1: Prepare human fecal cell suspension for
//   droplet cultivation. Single stool sample from FMT donor
//   (IRB 132-0212, University of Chicago). Aliquots spun
//   down in PBS, supernatant stored at -80 C. Live cell
//   density: 1e9/mL; dead cell density: 3e9/mL (BacLight
//   Live/Dead assay). Dilute 200x for Poisson-based single-
//   cell encapsulation (~20-30% droplets with 1 live cell).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Three separate stool aliquots dispensed -- one per media arm.
// Each aliquot is an independent 200x-diluted glycerol stock
// unit; dispensing separately avoids reuse of a consumed variable
// across the three parallel cultivation branches.
humanStoolBhis   = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
humanStoolGmm    = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
humanStoolYcfa   = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 2: Generate BHIS droplets from human stool.
//   Brain Heart Infusion Supplemented (BHIS) medium: 500 mL
//   water, 18.5 g BHI broth, 2.5 g yeast extract, 0.25 g
//   L-cysteine, vitamin K (0.1% in 95% ethanol), hemin
//   (5 mg/mL in 0.1 M NaOH). Spread 100 uL stool on agar
//   plates (parallel control, 7-day culture). Droplets:
//   0.5-1 mL emulsion of ~65-115 pL droplets (4-15 million
//   droplets). Incubate 2 days for droplets, 7 days for plates.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisMedium       = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
bhisOil          = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
bhisSuspension   = mix humanStoolBhis with bhisMedium for 2s
bhisDroplets     = mix bhisSuspension with bhisOil for 3s

heat bhisDroplets at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 3: Generate GMM droplets from human stool.
//   Gut Microbiota Medium (GMM) prepared per Goodman et al.
//   2011 (PNAS 108:6252). Second arm of parallel cultivation.
//   Incubate 2 days inside anaerobic chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

gmmMedium        = dispense 1 units of GMM_Medium
gmmOil           = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
gmmSuspension    = mix humanStoolGmm with gmmMedium for 2s
gmmDroplets      = mix gmmSuspension with gmmOil for 3s

heat gmmDroplets at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 4: Generate YCFA droplets from human stool.
//   Yeast Casitones Fatty Acid (YCFA, modified DSMZ 1611):
//   10 g casitone, 2.5 g yeast extract, 5 g dextrose,
//   short-chain fatty acids (acetic, propionic, isobutyric,
//   n-valeric, iso-valeric acids), NaHCO3, L-cysteine-HCl,
//   hemin, mucin, vitamin solution (biotin, folate,
//   pyridoxine-HCl, thiamine-HCl, riboflavin, nicotinic
//   acid, pantothenate, B12, PABA, thioctic acid).
//   pH 6.7-6.8. Incubate 2 days inside anaerobic chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ycfaMedium       = dispense 1 units of YCFA_Medium
ycfaOil          = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
ycfaSuspension   = mix humanStoolYcfa with ycfaMedium for 2s
ycfaDroplets     = mix ycfaSuspension with ycfaOil for 3s

heat ycfaDroplets at 37c for 2880m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 5: Break emulsions and extract DNA from all
//   three droplet cultures. Add equal part PFO to emulsion,
//   vortex and centrifuge, remove oil+PFO phase. Extract
//   DNA from aqueous layer using DNeasy Blood & Tissue Kit
//   (Qiagen); total elution volume: 100 uL per sample.
//   16S V4 amplicon sequencing (Illumina MiSeq 2x300,
//   primers from Caporaso et al. 2012) performed at Argonne
//   National Laboratory ESPSF. 35 PCR cycles; paired-end
//   joining in illumina-utils (min overlap 45 nt, <2
//   mismatches); ASVs inferred by MED/oligotyping v2.1;
//   taxonomy by GAST.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisBreaker      = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
gmmBreaker       = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
ycfaBreaker      = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent

bhisBroken       = mix bhisDroplets with bhisBreaker for 2s
gmmBroken        = mix gmmDroplets with gmmBreaker for 2s
ycfaBroken       = mix ycfaDroplets with ycfaBreaker for 2s

bhisKit          = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
gmmKit           = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
ycfaKit          = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit

bhisDNA          = mix bhisBroken with bhisKit for 30m
gmmDNA           = mix gmmBroken with gmmKit for 30m
ycfaDNA          = mix ycfaBroken with ycfaKit for 30m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 2, STEP 6: 16S rRNA amplicon sequencing of all
//   three media conditions. MED decomposition identifies
//   ASVs with single-nucleotide resolution. Richness (R),
//   Shannon index (H'), and low-abundance ASV count (Rlow,
//   for ASVs < 1% in raw stool) computed per sample.
//   Expected: 37% (BHIS) to 410% (YCFA) richness increase
//   in droplets vs. agar plates (p < 0.005, Mann-Whitney U).
//   Bacteroides oligotype clustering closer to raw stool
//   in droplet cultures (p < 0.005, multiscale bootstrap).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bhisProfile      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on bhisDNA for 30s
gmmProfile       = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on gmmDNA for 30s
ycfaProfile      = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on ycfaDNA for 30s

// Combine media profiles for richness QC gate.
// richnessSignal > 0 confirms droplets exceed plates in
// community richness across all three media conditions.
combinedProfiles   = mix bhisProfile with gmmProfile for 5s
richnessMeasure    = mix combinedProfiles with ycfaProfile for 5s
richnessSignal     = detect colonyDensityDetection on richnessMeasure for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Richness QC gate
// Pass (BB2): richnessSignal > 0 -> droplet richness confirmed
//             greater than plate richness across media;
//             proceed to slow-grower sorting (Phase 3).
// Fail (BB3): richnessSignal <= 0 -> no richness advantage
//             detected; drain cultivation output.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (richnessJoin).
// ============================================================

if (richnessSignal > 0) {
    dispose bhisDNA
    dispose gmmDNA
    dispose ycfaDNA
} else {
    drain bhisDNA
    drain gmmDNA
    drain ycfaDNA
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: richnessJoin
// Dispose richness QC measurements. Control passes to
// Phase 3 slow-grower sorting branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose richnessSignal
dispose bhisProfile
dispose gmmProfile
dispose ycfaProfile

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3, STEP 1: Prepare fresh BHIS droplet emulsion for
//   wavelet OD-based slow-grower sorting. Two independent
//   sorting experiments performed on human stool in BHIS
//   droplets. Droplets reinjected at 20 uL/hr with oil
//   spacing phase at 180 uL/hr. High-frame-rate camera
//   (Basler acA640-750um, 925 Hz, 672x360 px, 59 us exposure)
//   captures droplet image at sorting junction. Custom
//   LabView code applies biorthogonal 3.1 discrete wavelet
//   frame decomposition (Low Low High subband, 15x15 px
//   window, step 5 px, 15 gray levels, 3x3 px displacement).
//   Wavelet OD normalized 0 (empty) to 1 (dense colony).
//   Slow-growing colonies: 0.3 < waveletOD < 0.7.
//   Dense colonies: waveletOD > 0.7 -> waste path.
//   Empty droplets: waveletOD < 0.3 -> waste path.
//   Sorting rate: ~30 Hz. Electrode actuation: 10 kHz,
//   800 V p-p, 30% duty cycle, 10 ms per sort event.
//   False-positive sorting rate: at most 8% upper bound.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortingStool     = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
bhisSortMedium   = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
bhisSortOil      = dispense 1 units of HFE7500_Surfactant
sortSuspension   = mix sortingStool with bhisSortMedium for 2s
sortDroplets     = mix sortSuspension with bhisSortOil for 3s

heat sortDroplets at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 3, STEP 2: Image-based sorting via wavelet OD.
//   colonyDensityDetection module abstracts LabView wavelet
//   image analysis and electrode deflection of slow-growers
//   into the "keep" path. Sorted fraction: ~1-10 uL total
//   volume (thin layer on oil; estimated by pipetting).
//   Sorting signal > 0 indicates slow-growing colonies
//   detected and successfully deflected to keep channel.
//   Expected amplification: 6.5 ASVs amplified from <1% to
//   >1% (unsorted) vs. 12.5 ASVs (sorted) out of 158 total
//   ASVs; taxa span wider phylogenetic range after sorting.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortingSignal = detect colonyDensityDetection on sortDroplets for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Sorting QC gate
// Pass (BB5): sortingSignal > 0 -> slow-growing colonies
//             detected in keep path; proceed to DNA extraction
//             and viability confirmation (Phase 4).
// Fail (BB6): sortingSignal <= 0 -> no qualifying low-density
//             droplets found; drain sorted emulsion.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (sortingJoin).
// ============================================================

if (sortingSignal > 0) {
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    // PHASE 3, STEP 3 (pass path): Break sorted droplet emulsion
    //   and extract DNA. Due to low sorting rate (~30 Hz) the
    //   total sorted volume is only ~1-10 uL. Add 150 uL DNA-
    //   free water + 150 uL PFO to sorted emulsion, vortex,
    //   centrifuge. Extract with DNeasy kit. Sequence with same
    //   16S V4 protocol as unsorted samples. Kolmogorov-Smirnov
    //   test confirms shift in rank-abundance distribution
    //   between sorted and unsorted (p < 0.005).
    // ------------------------------------------------------------
    sortedBreaker    = dispense 1 units of PFO_BreakingAgent
    sortedKit        = dispense 1 units of DNAExtractionKit
    sortedBroken     = mix sortDroplets with sortedBreaker for 2s
    sortedDNA        = mix sortedBroken with sortedKit for 30m
    sortedProfile    = detect sixteenSrRNASequencing on sortedDNA for 30s
    dispose sortedDNA
    dispose sortedProfile
} else {
    drain sortDroplets
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: sortingJoin
// Dispose sorting QC signal. Control passes to Phase 4
// viability confirmation branch (BB8/BB9).
// ============================================================

dispose sortingSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PHASE 4, STEP 1: Confirm bacterial viability post-sorting.
//   Streak ~10 uL sorted droplet emulsion + oil onto BHIS
//   agar plate. Culture at 37 C for 2 days (2880 min).
//   Random picking of 24 colonies for Sanger sequencing
//   (27F/1492R primers, GoTaq Green Master Mix, 95 C 3 min;
//   30 cycles: 95 C 30 s, 54 C 30 s, 72 C 1 min; 72 C 10 min).
//   16S amplicons excised from 2% agarose gel, purified with
//   QIAquick Gel Extraction Kit (Qiagen), Sanger sequenced
//   (U. Chicago Comprehensive Cancer Center facility).
//   BLAST taxonomy assignment: Hafnia (12/24), Enterococcus
//   (8/24), Bacteroides (4/24).
//   FDA/PI live-dead staining (BacLight, ThermoFisher) used
//   as viability readout proxy in dropletViabilityDetection.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sortedForViability  = dispense 1 units of FetalCellSuspension
bhisAgarMedium      = dispense 1 units of BHIS_Medium
platedSorted        = mix sortedForViability with bhisAgarMedium for 2s

heat platedSorted at 37c for 2880m

fdaPI_Stain         = dispense 1 units of FDA_PI_Stain
stainedPlated       = mix platedSorted with fdaPI_Stain for 10m

viabilitySignal     = detect dropletViabilityDetection on stainedPlated for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB8 / BB9: Viability confirmation gate
// Pass (BB8): viabilitySignal > 0 -> colonies viable post-
//             sorting (Hafnia, Enterococcus, Bacteroides
//             confirmed by Sanger sequencing); dispose.
// Fail (BB9): viabilitySignal <= 0 -> no viable growth
//             observed on agar; drain.
// Both branches converge at BB10 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (viabilitySignal > 0) {
    dispose stainedPlated
    dispose platedSorted
} else {
    drain stainedPlated
    drain platedSorted
}

// ============================================================
// BB10: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all remaining QC signal droplets.
// Experiment ends. Pure strain isolates confirmed viable
// and compatible with downstream microbiology workflows.
// ============================================================

dispose viabilitySignal
dispose asfComposition
dispose asfDNA
dispose richnessMeasure
dispose combinedProfiles

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
